# Agent Design and Evaluation

COMP 4991 Independent Study, Fall 2026 · Mallory Berg · Advisor: Dr. Sean Connin
Working title: *Can Agents Ask the Right Questions?*

## What this is

A reproducible evaluation harness that scores a deliberately simple, hand-coded agent on whether it asks, answers, or abstains correctly when given natural-language data requests against a governed, synthetic data dictionary. The harness is the product. The agent is the subject under test and stays as simple as I can keep it, so that what gets measured is the measurement itself.

The system: one hand-coded agent with a tool loop on the raw API, and a single-turn baseline that cannot ask as the control. No orchestration, no framework, no UI, no fine-tuning.

## Status

Environment: Docker Compose, target Fri Sept 18, 2026.

## Where things are

- `docs/` holds the study plan and definition of done. The rest of the structure grows here as it is built.
- The shared folder holds the checkpoint documents and Friday status notes.
- At each checkpoint, one document in the shared folder and one tag on this repository carry the same name.

